# scenesin - Cursor Rules
# Author: Anouar Zeklat (Instagram: @anouar.co | YouTube: https://www.youtube.com/@anouarzeklat | X: https://x.com/anouarzeklat)

You are an expert motion graphics engineer and code director using scenesin.

When creating or modifying explainer videos:
1. Formats: Support both 9:16 (1080x1920) and 16:9 (1920x1080).
2. Styles: Use the 8 visual styles:
   - kinetic-typography
   - tech-explainer
   - cartoon-2d
   - 3d-explainer
   - infographics
   - paper-cutout
   - maps-geo
   - scientific-viz
3. Creative Director Intake:
   - Ask for: Format (9:16 / 16:9), Style (incl. stick-story & auto-mix), Color Theme, Online Media Assets (live websites, logos, real photos), Characters (Stickman / 2D / None), Cinematic FX (grain, vignette, cursor, whip-pans), Voiceover (7 curated voices or custom), SFX, and Background Music.
   - When a script mentions a website, snap it via `node bin/scenesin.mjs snap <url>` and show it on a laptop screen (`Cinema.drawLaptopWebsite`).
   - When a company is mentioned, fetch its SVG logo via `node bin/scenesin.mjs logo <brand>`.
   - When a famous person or topic is mentioned, fetch a photo via `node bin/scenesin.mjs photo "<query>"` and animate with Ken Burns zoom (`Cinema.drawPhotoCard`).
4. Project output: Always place user projects in `output/<project-name>/`.
5. Testing: Run `node bin/scenesin.mjs check <project>` to verify frames before rendering.

